Apply order 0039 against mariopartyrd/partyboard 98ac07fd1e8f7ab938bbb6fe75789fad99419010 (CC0-1.0; ADR 0009 section 5).
m445dll: the mole process starts over when its loop ends, as on the console, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

M4-07 (E2 game-side proof). Bowser Bop's mole process (fn_1_1C64) leaves its while (TRUE) loop with
break once the 60 s timer has run out (lbl_1_bss_6DC >= 4) and falls off the end of the function. On the
console a process starts through gclongjmp with LR set to its entry, so a function that returns
re-enters at its start: it clears its mole's flags and waits for a pop-up that never comes. Our
coroutines have no such return address, and src/libco.c panics ("a process coroutine returned"), which
faulted every E2 run of the minigame near its end. On MPT_PC the function now jumps back to its start
instead of returning. Bowser Bop is reached from Mini-game mode and Story only, never from a party, so
no committed replay or golden plays this code; state hashes do not move (docs/titles/mp4.md, M1).

